{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"batch_notes\":[\"The batch contains one available dossier, so cross-ruler calibration is limited; the common rubric anchors were applied, but no other available dossier job key exists for calibrated_against.\",\"The evidence supports a severe authoritarian-rule judgment through Xi-attributed authority centralization, loyalist appointment and party-state reorganization, reinforced by censorship, coercive legal controls, and an extremely low press-freedom ranking.\",\"Institutional and personal attribution are not identical: several adverse events are documented at the party-state or security-institution level rather than by a direct Xi order.\"],\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2023-population-top20-gate1-judges-v2:2023:4B\",\"chapter_id\":\"4B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"calibrated_against\":[],\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2023-population-top20-gate1-judges-v2:2023:4B\",\"chapter_id\":\"4B\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Xi Jinping's 2023 political-freedom record fits the severe-authoritarian 2–3 anchor. Direct evidence attributes Xi with a governing structure centered on his authority and with appointing close supporters while transferring important portfolios toward party organs (E016, E017). The same period shows censorship of investigative reporting, coercive counter-espionage enforcement, detention and disappearance of critics, and China ranked 179th of 180 for press freedom (E011, E013, E018, E019). These mechanisms jointly indicate narrow and risky opposition, weak independent constraints, extensive information control, and limited tolerance for dissent. The score is not reduced to 1 because the dossier does not establish Xi's personal order or corrective responsibility for every abuse, and it contains some positive official child-development outcomes that do not materially offset the political-freedom evidence (E015).\",\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"Political freedom was weaker in 2023 under Xi-centered party control, censorship, and coercive legal and security practices; no evidence shows strengthening of contestability or independent constraints.\"}],\"confidence_score\":0.86,\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E015\",\"explanation\":\"Official 2023 child-development indicators improved, but they do not establish political freedom, equitable civic access, or Xi-specific democratic restraint.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E011\",\"explanation\":\"The documented disappearances, detentions, and sentences establish institutional conduct more securely than Xi's personal direction or knowledge.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E018\",\"explanation\":\"Counter-Espionage Law enforcement can be presented by Chinese authorities as national-security policy, creating an interpretive caveat even though the effects on civic and informational space are adverse.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E016\",\"explanation\":\"The 2023 economic team was composed of close Xi supporters and reorganization shifted important portfolios toward party organs, directly indicating ruler-attributed party capture and reduced institutional autonomy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E017\",\"explanation\":\"An official 2023 government report explicitly placed governance under the Central Committee with Xi Jinping at its core, directly evidencing concentrated personal authority.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E013\",\"explanation\":\"Investigative reports on an alleged death in police custody were deleted in June 2023, demonstrating constrained investigative journalism and censorship during the target period.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E018\",\"explanation\":\"Vague Counter-Espionage Law amendments and raids on Mintz and Bain created coercive uncertainty and administrative pressure affecting independent information and civic space.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E019\",\"explanation\":\"China ranked 179th of 180 in the 2023 World Press Freedom Index and was described as the world's largest captor of journalists and press-freedom defenders.\"}],\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[],\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2023-population-top20-gate1-v2:2023:CHN:15833\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"Scores 4 or above are rejected because the evidence does not show meaningful political competition, independent oversight, protected media space, or credible constraints operating alongside authoritarian control. Scores 8 or above are especially unavailable because there is no affirmative evidence of ruler-attributed self-binding or strengthening of contestability, civic space, or transfer rules.\",\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"China entered 2023 with an established centralized party-state and restricted political-freedom baseline. That inherited condition is context, not itself a Xi score. The 2023 evidence shows Xi-centered formal authority and party reorganization, while many coercive acts were carried out by state or security institutions under mediated rather than personally documented attribution.\",\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"iso3\":\"CHN\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"Score 1 is rejected because the dossier does not prove that Xi personally ordered every documented detention, disappearance, censorship action, or abuse, and the evidence set includes some positive state outcomes. Nonetheless, the ruler-attributed concentration of authority and documented systemic restrictions clearly place the case above the absolute lowest anchor.\",\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_required\":false,\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"4B.2: direct evidence of Xi personally manipulating electoral rules, courts, election commissions, or security forces for entrenchment is limited, though party-state reorganization is relevant.\",\"4B.8: succession, term-limit, and constitutional-transfer evidence for 2023 is absent.\",\"4B.7: minority and excluded-group evidence is primarily institutional rather than directly personal.\",\"4B.10: inherited-to-2023 trajectory is inferential because the dossier lacks a detailed baseline comparison.\"],\"period_end_year\":2023,\"period_start_year\":2023,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":2.0,\"upper\":3.5},\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_4b_v3\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Direct attribution is strongest for Xi-centered authority and loyalist appointments/reorganization (E016, E017) and for Xi's public characterization of Xinjiang policy as successful (E012). Censorship, detention, counter-espionage enforcement, and press restrictions are more securely attributed to the party-state and security institutions, with no direct Xi order established for each event.\",\"ruler_id\":\"1432\",\"ruler_name\":\"Xi Jinping\",\"ruler_year_id\":15833,\"score_1_to_10\":2.5,\"source_mix\":\"Human Rights Watch; Reporters Without Borders; official Chinese government and National Bureau of Statistics records; specialist political analysis. The mix includes strong event-specific NGO and press-freedom evidence, official records useful for formal authority and reported outcomes, and qualified analytical interpretation. Source-family overlap and institutional-versus-personal attribution limits are retained.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Local structured priors were available for all ten lenses, based on 2023 political-freedom country-year facts covering civil liberties, expression, association, media, voice, accountability, and rule of law. They function as contextual priors; the chapter score rests on cited ruler-period evidence, especially E016, E017, E013, E018, and E019.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"4B.1\",\"4B.2\",\"4B.3\",\"4B.4\",\"4B.5\",\"4B.6\",\"4B.7\",\"4B.8\",\"4B.9\",\"4B.10\"]}],\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2023-population-top20-gate1-judges-v2:2023:4B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_4b_v3\",\"run_key\":\"2023-population-top20-gate1-judges-v2\",\"run_profile\":{\"dossier_count\":1,\"model\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"provider\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"provider_profile\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"unavailable_dossier_count\":0,\"usage\":{\"estimated_cost_usd\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"input_tokens\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"output_tokens\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"total_tokens\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\"}},\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"target_year\":2023,\"unavailable_dossiers\":[]}"}}
